      {
        "by": "FarhanAliRaza",
        "outdated": false,
        "first_comment": "This also catches `StateSchemaMismatchError`. `BaseState._deserialize` raises it when a state class gains or loses a field. That is a normal event in dev mode, and the disk manager is the dev default."
      },
      {
        "by": "FarhanAliRaza",
        "outdated": false,
        "first_comment": "Please remove the redaction, the whitespace collapse and the 512-char cap. Pickle and schema errors do not contain the client token. They contain module, attribute or byte details. The Redis manager a"
      },
      {
        "by": "FarhanAliRaza",
        "outdated": false,
        "first_comment": "The format gives broken output. An exception message that ends with a period gives a double period: `invalid load key, 'n'.. Falling back\u2026`. An empty message gives `StateSchemaMismatchError: . Falling"
      },
      {
        "by": "FarhanAliRaza",
        "outdated": false,
        "first_comment": "The app recovers with a default state, so this is a warning, not an error. Please use `logger.warning`."
      },
      {
        "by": "FarhanAliRaza",
        "outdated": false,
        "first_comment": "Please keep the existing tests unchanged. The switch from `\"client\"` to `CLIENT_ID` is not related to this fix. Inline the literals in the new tests."
      },
      {
        "by": "FarhanAliRaza",
        "outdated": false,
        "first_comment": "These two asserts check wording that the log never had. Please remove them. Also, the four new tests copy the same `caplog` filter. Please move it into one helper."
      }
    ]
  },
